{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Cross-source audit finding (2026-07-30): this is NOT confined to the weekly canary — the same failure is hitting the on-demand `Live External Integration` workflow, and it failed **every** run dispatched today.\n\nAll 6 `Live External Integration` runs on 2026-07-30 failed (UTC):\n  02:10:36 (30507727332), 02:37:12 (30508956696), 03:59:13 (30512622682),\n  05:05:12 (30515632763), 18:59:36 (30572868192), 19:46:17 (30576261975)\nOver the 7-day window I inventoried (2026-07-23 -> 07-30, 2,598 Actions runs) there were 7 failures of this workflow and no successes.\n\nVerbatim from run 30576261975, job \"external integration (live services)\":\n\n    rebar._snapshot.repo_snapshot.SnapshotRefError: cannot resolve ref 'HEAD' to a commit in\n    '/home/runner/work/_temp/rebar-basetemp/test_live_plan_review_workflow0/repo'. Name a valid\n    branch, tag, or full SHA reachable from 'origin'. Fetching an arbitrary SHA also requires the\n    remote's uploadpack.allowReachableSHA1InWant (or fetch a containing ref then resolve).\n      src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:377: SnapshotRefError\n\n    7 failed, 21 passed, 1 skipped, 1 xfailed, 1 warning in 101.45s (0:01:41)\n\nThe 7 failing tests are consistent across runs:\n  tests/external/test_execution_mode_live.py::test_single_turn_live_structured_output\n  tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py::test_pydantic_review_ticket_opus\n  tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py::test_pydantic_review_code\n  tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py::test_pydantic_scan_spec\n  tests/external/test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py::test_pydantic_verify_completion\n  tests/external/test_workflow_live.py::test_live_review_skeleton_workflow_end_to_end\n  tests/external/test_workflow_live.py::test_live_plan_review_workflow_engine_produces_real_verdict\n\nTwo other jobs in the same runs also fail — \"langfuse tracing round-trip (ephemeral self-hosted)\" in every case, and \"jira DC harness smoke\" in run 30572868192. I did not determine whether those share this root cause or are independent; worth checking before scoping the fix, since a fix targeting only the snapshot path may leave the workflow red.\n\nScope note for the ticket title: \"weekly canary red since 2026-07-14\" understates it — the failure reproduces on every dispatch, so it is continuous, not weekly."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785451603957211001,"uuid":"af0f34ca-793d-4b2c-ad56-000177addfa4"}